  Member form for the 8 Activity fields: written as "Activity.Field__c", NOT "Task.Field__c".
  These fields are declared under objects/Activity/fields/ and federate onto both Task and Event;
  this repo's own manifest/package.xml already uses this exact form for the SAME fields in its
  CustomField constructive block (verified: manifest/package.xml pre-edit lines 244-251), and the
  design's own Section 2.4 states this explicitly. (Permission-set fieldPermissions grants, by
  contrast, correctly use "Task.Field__c" / "Event.Field__c" - a permission set is not deploying
  the field itself, it is granting FLS on a Task/Event row, and Activity is not a valid SObject
  prefix there - see Broker_Protection_Access.permissionset-meta.xml precedent cited in the design.)

  Ordering note: Salesforce resolves dependency order WITHIN a single destructive-changes payload
  automatically (all members here are submitted as one transaction) - the step ordering in the
  design's Section 5 (list view before fields; TaskFanoutService before Tasks_Fanned_Out__c; etc.)
  governs which components must NOT be split across separate deploys, not the line order within
  this file. Since the user has waived the Wave 1 / Wave 2 rollback boundary and asked for one
  combined payload, every constraint the design listed as "same payload" is satisfied by merging
  into ONE manifest deploy - do not further subdivide into the design's original Steps 1 through 6
  unless the combined deploy fails and a staged retry is needed for diagnosis.

